    "default_visible": false,
    "default_opacity": 0.75,
    "legend_note": "The sector that residents work in more than France as a whole does, measured as a multiple of its national share. Colour saturation shows how strongly it stands out: pale at 1.5× the national share, full colour at 6× or more. Below 1.5× nothing stands out and the commune is plain gray (Mixed). It shows what is distinctive, not what is biggest: nearly everywhere, most people work in public services and shops. Much of rural France reads Agriculture even though farmers are a minority there, because nationally they are 2%. In ski country Transport can win: INSEE classes lift operators as land transport. Blank under 200 residents in work, where the census sample is too small to compare eleven shares."
  },
